# Start the boot splash as soon as a DRM device exists. This is the whole trigger: the initrd
# carries no GPU driver any more, so the first card node appears after switch-root when udev
# autoloads amdgpu/i915/xe/nvidia/virtio_gpu, and that is exactly the moment the systemd-stub
# bitmap stops being scanned out.
#
# ACTION=="add" only, deliberately NOT "add|change". A card emits `change` whenever a connector
# is hotplugged — every monitor plugged into a running desktop — and each one would be a fresh
# start request for a unit that has long since exited, i.e. a boot splash painted over somebody's
# session. Cards themselves are added once, and udev replays `add` at coldplug, so nothing is
# missed by leaving `change` out.
#
# The splash is safe against a spurious late start anyway, and by construction rather than by
# luck: it takes DRM master before it draws anything, and a running compositor already holds it,
# so the attempt fails and the program exits without touching the screen. This rule narrows the
# window; that is what closes it.
#
# Render nodes (renderD*) are skipped: they cannot modeset.
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="drm", KERNEL=="card[0-9]*", TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="@DISTRO_ID@-splash.service"
